{{also|abel}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|he}} {{term|הבל||tr=hebel, hevel|breath, vapor; vanity|lang=he}} or from {{etyl|akk}} {{term||tr=aplu||son}}{{rfscript|Cuneiform}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeɪbəl/}}
* {{homophones|able}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{biblical character}} The son of [[Adam]] and [[Eve]] who was killed by his brother [[Cain]].
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version|Genesis|4|8}}:
#*: And Cain talked with '''Abel''' his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against '''Abel''' his brother, and slew him.
# {{given name|male|from=Hebrew}}.

